{
  "id": "31662_yopparau",
  "headword": "{酔|よ}っぱらう",
  "reading": "よっぱらう",
  "romaji": "yopparau",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to get drunk",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to get drunk; to be drunk",
      "explanation": "To become thoroughly drunk, more emphatic and more colloquial than {酔|よ}う. The state is expressed with the ている form: {酔|よ}っぱらっている (is drunk)."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "31662_yopparau_ex1",
      "japanese": "⟦{父|ちち}→父：00566_chichi⟧⟦は→は：00079_ha⟧{酔|よ}っぱらって⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧。",
      "english": "My father is drunk.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "31662_yopparau_ex2",
      "japanese": "⟦{昨日|きのう}→昨日：00859_kinou⟧⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{夜|よる}→夜：00487_yoru⟧⟦は→は：00079_ha⟧⟦すっかり→すっかり：01270_sukkari⟧{酔|よ}っぱらった。",
      "english": "Last night I got completely drunk.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "31662_yopparau_ex3",
      "japanese": "{酔|よ}っぱらって⟦{電車|でんしゃ}→電車：00522_densha⟧⟦で→で：00502_de⟧⟦{寝|ね}て→寝る：00470_neru⟧しまい、⟦{終点|しゅうてん}→終点：05457_shuuten⟧⟦まで→まで：00490_made⟧⟦{行|い}って→行く：00119_iku⟧しまった。",
      "english": "I got drunk, fell asleep on the train and ended up at the last stop.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Also written {酔|よ}っ{払|ぱら}う. The noun {酔|よ}っぱらい (a drunk) is very common.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦すっかり→すっかり：01270_sukkari⟧ / ⟦べろべろ→べろべろ：09428_berobero⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{酔|よ}っぱらう: to get completely / blind drunk\n- {酔|よ}っぱらって⟦{帰|かえ}る→帰る：00508_kaeru⟧: to come home drunk\n- {酔|よ}っぱらい⟦{運転|うんてん}→運転：01335_unten⟧: drunk driving (everyday word; the legal term is ⟦{飲酒運転|いんしゅうんてん}→飲酒運転：18486_inshuunten⟧)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{酔|よ}う→酔う：14437_you⟧: to get drunk; also to get carsick or seasick — neutral, wider\n- ⟦ほろ{酔|よ}い→ほろ酔い：09370_horoyoi⟧: tipsy, pleasantly a little drunk",
